A mistake of fact at the time of acquisition: the acquirer believes he is acquiring ownership.
• In good faith is someone who
  – acquires from a person with capacity without knowing that this person is not owner/lacks authority of disposal (Modestinus D 50.16.109, Case 80);
  – acquires from a PUPILLUS/FURIOSUS/PRODIGUS without knowing of the lack of capacity;
  – acquires from an unauthorised person without a valid title, unaware of both defects (putative title).
• A mistake of law excludes BONA FIDES.
